Every clinician should discuss an intentional-or-unintentional-unprescribed-person-opioid-sharing-risk-for-household-or-other-person with a patient.
Every clinician should discuss a shared-opioid-overdose-at-same-or-lower-dosage-risk with a patient.
Every clinician should discuss a young-child-or-pet-unintentional-opioid-ingestion-risk with a patient.
Every unprescribed-shared-opioid-recipient can possibly experience an overdose at a same-or-lower-dosage.
Every young-child can possibly experience an unintentional-opioid-ingestion.
Every pet can possibly experience an unintentional-opioid-ingestion.
